# Marker OFI event-time selection

## Pre-work Plan

- Background: Daedalus true SPAA on final local graph reports entry marker exists, but hovering its 22:01 event inside a 60K candle leaves `ta-row-ofi-band-price-60k` at `data-marker-event-count=0` until timeout.
- Goal: Make marker interaction select the marker's accepted canonical placement/event-time for OFI without a second row-axis snap.
- Assumptions: Marker placement is already validated against its target candle/position; the renderer owns interaction projection, while marker Label/Tooltip remain the existing generic payload.
- Scope: Renderer marker interaction/cursor projection, focused model tests, BrowserDemo fixture, F# Playwright and immutable Renderer/Interactive package closure. No wire/domain/provider changes.
- Acceptance: A marker at 22:01 inside a 60K bar directly populates the 60K OFI band on hover; normal plot hover still follows row axis; shared cursor callback uses marker event time; existing 4,000-bar/OFI/performance gates pass.
- Risk: Forcing row-wide cursor state from a marker may update unrelated rows inconsistently or trigger provider actions; event handling must remain bounded and generation-safe.
- Stop condition: New immutable candidate passes owner gates and Daedalus true SPAA clean-cache gate.

